      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R72", "R35", "REG2"],
      "pins": ["REG2.24"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0142", "GND"],
      "observed": "The MIC26903 feedback divider uses R72 = 19.6 kΩ and R35 = 1.3 kΩ. With the drawn feedback relation, this gives approximately 12.9 V, not the +5 V rail shown.",
      "expected": "The feedback-divider ratio should set REG2 to approximately 5 V; with a 1.3 kΩ lower resistor, the upper resistor would need to be about 5.5 kΩ.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "REG2 MIC26903YJL-TR; pin 24 FB is NET0142; R72 19k6; R35 1k3; Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6); +5V (Power sheet, page 1/6)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "A MIC26903YJL-TR buck regulator steps the battery input down to 5 V. (Design specification, §4)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The regulator may produce a substantially overvoltage rail instead of 5 V, potentially damaging or disrupting the 5 V loads and the 3.3 V regulator fed from that rail.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The MIC26903 feedback-divider values appear inconsistent with the specified 5 V output: 19.6 kΩ and 1.3 kΩ imply about 12.9 V using the schematic's feedback relation."
}

